# Ignore the whole build context, then allow back only what the image needs.
# A blacklist lets the next private file added to .gitignore slip in through
# ADD . — the image is built by allowing named things in, not by naming the
# things to keep out. The container loads the gem from lib/ and runs the
# generators in dev/ against docs mounted at run time, so nothing here needs
# docs/, the git history or its rewrite scratch, editor and agent files
# (.claude, CLAUDE.md, .solargraph.yml, .rubocop.yml), caches, logs, tmp/,
# built gems, or .DS_Store.
*
!lib
!bin
!dev
!fonts
!Gemfile
!rsyntaxtree.gemspec
!Rakefile
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!LICENSE
